# nested working clones / arm worktrees — each has its own git
case*/upstream/
case*/arms/
# sealed ground truth (seeded-bug answer keys): NEVER in the repo — the
# ledger carries only the sha256; the orchestrator stays blind until grading
case*/sealed/
# raw headless outputs can be large; ledger/raw is tracked selectively
*.wasm
*.szx
__pycache__/
case*/paper/*.aux
case*/paper/*.log
case*/paper/*.out

# Manuscripts.
# 2026-08-06 (operator): ARTICLE.md and REPORT.md are LOCAL ONLY, never published
#   to the remote.
# 2026-08-29 (operator): REVERSED for ARTICLE.md. Nothing is under submission or
#   will be for now, so no venue preprint policy is at risk, and the root
#   ARTICLE.md had already published every headline number these two elaborate.
#   case01 and case02 ARTICLE.md are now tracked deliberately. This does NOT
#   auto-publish a future case's article: dropping the rule only means a new
#   ARTICLE.md appears untracked in `git status` instead of being hidden, and it
#   still needs an explicit `git add`.
# Still local, unchanged: REPORT.md (case01, case04) and every LaTeX build below
#   — the "IEEE build remains local for now" instruction stands.
case*/REPORT.md
case*/paper/
case*/paper_springer/*.aux
case*/paper_springer/*.log
case*/paper_springer/*.out
case*/paper_springer/*.bbl
case*/paper_springer/*.blg

# case02 grading: unblinding keys must never be committed
case*/grading/KEY_*.json
